{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"source .venv/bin/activate && python - << 'PY'\nimport json, os, datetime, pathlib, textwrap\nroot=pathlib.Path('.')\nmeta=json.load(open('artifacts/selected_papers_metadata.json'))\nds_summary=json.load(open('artifacts/dataset_summary.json'))\n\nrelevance={\n'Chain-of-Thought Prompting Elicits Reasoning in Large Language Models':'Foundational CoT prompting baseline and emergence behavior.',\n'Self-Consistency Improves Chain of Thought Reasoning in Language Models':'Canonical test-time compute baseline (sample multiple traces + vote).',\n'Tree of Thoughts: Deliberate Problem Solving with Large Language Models':'Structured search over reasoning traces; useful for adaptive trace budgeting.',\n\\\"Let's Verify Step by Step\\\":'Key process-supervision paper; directly links step-level supervision to robustness and OOD.',\n\\\"Chain-of-Thought Hub: A Continuous Effort to Measure Large Language Models' Reasoning Performance\\\":'Benchmark suite spanning GSM8K/MATH/BBH/MMLU for reasoning evaluation.',\n'Math-Shepherd: Verify and Reinforce LLMs Step-by-step without Human Annotations':'Automatic process reward construction; practical alternative to expensive human labels.',\n'Contrastive Chain-of-Thought Prompting':'Demonstrates learning from incorrect reasoning contrastively.',\n'GRACE: Discriminator-Guided Chain-of-Thought Reasoning':'Step-level discriminator guidance; helps reduce wrong reasoning branches.',\n'OCEAN: Offline Chain-of-thought Evaluation and Alignment in Large Language Models':'Offline CoT evaluator/alignment paradigm; relevant for verifier-based selection.',\n'Multi-Step Deductive Reasoning Over Natural Language: An Empirical Study on Out-of-Distribution Generalisation':'Direct OOD generalization study in multi-step reasoning.',\n'Chain-of-Thought Reasoning is a Policy Improvement Operator':'Theoretical/algorithmic framing of CoT as iterative policy improvement.',\n'Buffer of Thoughts: Thought-Augmented Reasoning with Large Language Models':'Template-buffer approach trading off quality and efficiency.',\n'Is Chain-of-Thought Reasoning of LLMs a Mirage? A Data Distribution Lens':'Strong evidence for distribution-dependent/non-monotonic CoT behavior.',\n'Slim-SC: Thought Pruning for Efficient Scaling with Self-Consistency':'Adaptive pruning for self-consistency, central to length/compute control.',\n'Sleep-time Compute: Beyond Inference Scaling at Test-time':'Alternative compute allocation (offline precomputation) for reasoning tasks.',\n'Towards Reasoning Era: A Survey of Long Chain-of-Thought for Reasoning Large Language Models':'Survey of long-CoT methods, risks, and open problems.',\n}\n\n# papers README\nlines=['# Downloaded Papers','']\nfor i,p in enumerate(meta,1):\n    fn=os.path.basename(p['file'])\n    arxiv=(p.get('id') or '').replace('v','') if p.get('id') else 'N/A'\n    lines.append(f\\\"{i}. [{p['title']}]({fn})\\\")\n    lines.append(f\\\"   - Authors: {', '.join(p.get('authors',[])[:8])}{' et al.' if len(p.get('authors',[]))>8 else ''}\\\")\n    lines.append(f\\\"   - Year: {p.get('year')}\\\")\n    lines.append(f\\\"   - arXiv: {p.get('url')}\\\")\n    lines.append(f\\\"   - Why relevant: {relevance.get(p['title'],'Relevant to reasoning trace control and robustness.')}\\\")\n    lines.append('')\n(root/'papers'/'README.md').write_text('\\\\n'.join(lines))\n\n# datasets .gitignore\n(root/'datasets'/'.gitignore').write_text(textwrap.dedent('''\\\\\n# Exclude all data files (can be large)\n*\n\n# But include documentation and small samples\n\"'!.gitignore\n!README.md\n!**/README.md\n!**/samples/\n!**/samples/**\n!**/download.sh\n!**/download_instructions.txt\n'\"'''))\n\n# datasets README\nds_readme=textwrap.dedent('''\\\\\n# Downloaded Datasets\n\nThis directory contains datasets for the research project. Large data files are not intended for git commits; keep them local and rely on the instructions below for reproducibility.\n\n## Dataset 1: GSM8K\n\n### Overview\n- **Source**: \"'`gsm8k` (`main` config) on Hugging Face\n- **Size**: train 7,473; test 1,319\n- **Format**: HuggingFace DatasetDict\n- **Task**: Math word-problem reasoning\n- **Splits**: train/test\n- **License**: Check dataset card on Hugging Face\n\n### Download Instructions\n\n**Using HuggingFace (recommended):**\n```python\nfrom datasets import load_dataset\ndataset = load_dataset(\"gsm8k\", \"main\")\ndataset.save_to_disk(\"datasets/gsm8k_main\")\n```\n\n### Loading the Dataset\n```python\nfrom datasets import load_from_disk\ndataset = load_from_disk(\"datasets/gsm8k_main\")\n```\n\n### Sample Data\nStored at `datasets/gsm8k_main/samples/samples.json`.\n\n### Notes\n- Strong base benchmark for chain-of-thought length and self-consistency studies.\n\n## Dataset 2: MATH-500\n\n### Overview\n- **Source**: `HuggingFaceH4/MATH-500`\n- **Size**: test 500\n- **Format**: HuggingFace DatasetDict\n- **Task**: Competition-level mathematical reasoning\n- **Splits**: test\n- **License**: Check dataset card on Hugging Face\n\n### Download Instructions\n\n**Using HuggingFace (recommended):**\n```python\nfrom datasets import load_dataset\ndataset = load_dataset(\"HuggingFaceH4/MATH-500\")\ndataset.save_to_disk(\"datasets/math500\")\n```\n\n### Loading the Dataset\n```python\nfrom datasets import load_from_disk\ndataset = load_from_disk(\"datasets/math500\")\n```\n\n### Sample Data\nStored at `datasets/math500/samples/samples.json`.\n\n### Notes\n- Useful hard evaluation set for testing whether optimal trace length shifts with problem difficulty.\n\n## Dataset 3: ARC-Challenge\n\n### Overview\n- **Source**: `allenai/ai2_arc` (`ARC-Challenge` config)\n- **Size**: train 1,119; validation 299; test 1,172\n- **Format**: HuggingFace DatasetDict\n- **Task**: Science QA reasoning / transfer-style robustness check\n- **Splits**: train/validation/test\n- **License**: Check dataset card on Hugging Face\n\n### Download Instructions\n\n**Using HuggingFace (recommended):**\n```python\nfrom datasets import load_dataset\ndataset = load_dataset(\"allenai/ai2_arc\", \"ARC-Challenge\")\ndataset.save_to_disk(\"datasets/ai2_arc_challenge\")\n```\n\n### Loading the Dataset\n```python\nfrom datasets import load_from_disk\ndataset = load_from_disk(\"datasets/ai2_arc_challenge\")\n```\n\n### Sample Data\nStored at `datasets/ai2_arc_challenge/samples/samples.json`.\n\n### Notes\n- Adds non-math domain shift, useful for OOD robustness tests.\n\n## Dataset 4-6: BBH Subset Tasks\n\n### Overview\n- **Source**: `lukaemon/bbh`\n- **Configs downloaded**: `multistep_arithmetic_two`, `logical_deduction_three_objects`, `date_understanding`\n- **Size**: each test split has 250 examples\n- **Format**: HuggingFace DatasetDict\n- **Task**: Diverse compositional reasoning stress tests\n\n### Download Instructions\n\n**Using HuggingFace (recommended):**\n```python\nfrom datasets import load_dataset\nfor cfg in [\n    \"multistep_arithmetic_two\",\n    \"logical_deduction_three_objects\",\n    \"date_understanding\",\n]:\n    ds = load_dataset(\"lukaemon/bbh\", cfg)\n    ds.save_to_disk(f\"datasets/bbh_{cfg}\")\n```\n\n### Loading the Dataset\n```python\nfrom datasets import load_from_disk\ndataset = load_from_disk(\"datasets/bbh_multistep_arithmetic_two\")\n```\n\n### Sample Data\nStored in each dataset folder under `samples/samples.json`.\n\n### Notes\n- BBH provides task diversity to test whether trace-length optima are task-dependent.\n'\"''')\n(root/'datasets'/'README.md').write_text(ds_readme)\n\n# code README\ncode_readme=textwrap.dedent('''\\\\\n# Cloned Repositories\n\n## Repo 1: chain-of-thought-hub\n- URL: https://github.com/FranxYao/chain-of-thought-hub\n- Purpose: Multi-benchmark CoT evaluation suite (GSM8K, MATH, BBH, MMLU).\n- Location: \"'`code/chain-of-thought-hub/`\n- Key files:\n  - `readme.md`\n  - `BBH/run_bbh.py`\n  - `MMLU/run_mmlu_open_source.py`\n- Notes: Provides prompt templates and benchmark runners useful for fixed-length and sampled-CoT baselines.\n\n## Repo 2: tree-of-thought-llm\n- URL: https://github.com/princeton-nlp/tree-of-thought-llm\n- Purpose: Official Tree-of-Thoughts implementation for deliberate inference-time search.\n- Location: `code/tree-of-thought-llm/`\n- Key files:\n  - `run.py`\n  - `scripts/game24/*.sh`\n  - `src/tot/`\n- Notes: Useful for adaptive reasoning budget baselines (branching/search depth controls).\n\n## Repo 3: prm800k\n- URL: https://github.com/openai/prm800k\n- Purpose: PRM800K process-supervision labels and evaluation logic from “Let’s Verify Step by Step”.\n- Location: `code/prm800k/`\n- Key files:\n  - `README.md`\n  - `prm800k/data/`\n  - `prm800k/eval/eval.py`\n- Notes: Includes step-level supervision data format, grading scripts, and PRM-vs-ORM evaluation setup.\n'\"''')\n(root/'code'/'README.md').write_text(code_readme)\n\n# literature_review.md\nlit=textwrap.dedent('''\\\\\n# Literature Review: Reasoning Trace Length as a Proxy for Robustness\n\n## Review Scope\n\n### Research Question\nHow does reasoning trace length affect OOD robustness in LLM reasoning, and can adaptive trace-length control outperform fixed-length strategies?\n\n### Inclusion Criteria\n- Studies on chain-of-thought, trace control, process supervision, verifier-guided reasoning, or test-time reasoning compute.\n- Studies reporting reasoning benchmark results (GSM8K, MATH, BBH, ARC-like transfers).\n- OOD/distribution-shift analyses or efficiency-accuracy tradeoff analyses.\n\n### Exclusion Criteria\n- Purely non-LLM symbolic systems without relevance to modern LLM trace control.\n- Papers lacking empirical evidence or clear methodological detail.\n\n### Time Frame\n2022-2025 (plus foundational context where required).\n\n### Sources\n- arXiv API (primary)\n- Semantic Scholar API (supplementary)\n- Paper-finder script attempted but service timed out in this run\n\n## Search Log\n\n| Date | Query | Source | Results | Notes |\n|------|-------|--------|---------|-------|\n| 2026-04-06 | \\\"Reasoning Trace Length as a Proxy for Robustness ...\\\" | paper-finder script | timeout | Fallback to manual APIs |\n| 2026-04-06 | chain of thought length / OOD reasoning / test-time compute | arXiv API | 100+ candidates | deduplicated and ranked |\n| 2026-04-06 | CoT robustness / OOD generalization | Semantic Scholar API | merged into candidate pool | used for citation/context |\n\n## Screening Results\n\n- Title/abstract screened: 101\n- Full PDFs downloaded: 16\n- Deep-read (all chunk PDFs):\n  - \"'`Let’s Verify Step by Step` (10 chunks)\n  - `Multi-Step Deductive Reasoning... OOD Generalisation` (6 chunks)\n  - `Is CoT a Mirage?` (13 chunks)\n\n## Key Papers\n\n### 1) Chain-of-Thought Prompting Elicits Reasoning in Large Language Models (2022)\n- **Key Contribution**: Establishes CoT prompting as a major reasoning boost.\n- **Methodology**: Few-shot CoT exemplars.\n- **Datasets**: Standard reasoning benchmarks (math/commonsense).\n- **Results**: Large gains vs direct answer prompting.\n- **Relevance**: Defines the baseline trace-length intervention.\n\n### 2) Self-Consistency Improves Chain of Thought Reasoning in Language Models (2022)\n- **Key Contribution**: Replaces greedy single-trace decoding with multi-trace sampling + voting.\n- **Methodology**: Sample diverse traces; marginalize answers.\n- **Datasets**: GSM8K, SVAMP, AQuA, StrategyQA, ARC-style sets (per paper).\n- **Results**: Stronger reasoning accuracy with added test-time compute.\n- **Relevance**: Central fixed-compute/variable-trace baseline for this project.\n\n### 3) Tree of Thoughts (2023)\n- **Key Contribution**: Search over thought states instead of pure left-to-right generation.\n- **Methodology**: Deliberate branching/evaluation/selection.\n- **Results**: Improved outcomes on planning/search-heavy tasks.\n- **Relevance**: Natural adaptive-length/control baseline.\n\n### 4) Let’s Verify Step by Step (2023)\n- **Key Contribution**: Process supervision outperforms outcome supervision.\n- **Methodology**: PRM vs ORM; step-level human labels (PRM800K), best-of-N search evaluation.\n- **Datasets Used**: MATH + held-out STEM OOD tests (AP Physics/Calculus/Chemistry, AMC10/12).\n- **Results**: Deep-read excerpts indicate PRM reaches ~78% solved on representative MATH subset and consistently beats ORM/majority-vote baselines; better OOD behavior than ORM.\n- **Relevance**: Direct evidence that *quality and selection* of traces matters more than raw verbosity.\n\n### 5) Chain-of-Thought Hub (2023)\n- **Key Contribution**: Open benchmark stack for reasoning models and prompts.\n- **Methodology**: Unified evaluation across GSM8K/MATH/BBH/MMLU etc.\n- **Relevance**: Practical infrastructure for controlled trace-length experiments.\n\n### 6) Math-Shepherd (2023)\n- **Key Contribution**: Automatic process reward model training without expensive human labeling.\n- **Relevance**: Scalable process-verifier signal for adaptive trace filtering.\n\n### 7) Contrastive Chain-of-Thought Prompting (2023)\n- **Key Contribution**: Uses negative reasoning examples to reduce typical CoT mistakes.\n- **Relevance**: Supports the view that trace content quality, not just length, drives robustness.\n\n### 8) GRACE (2023)\n- **Key Contribution**: Step-level correctness discriminator guides decoding.\n- **Relevance**: Verifier-guided adaptive pruning strategy.\n\n### 9) OCEAN (2024)\n- **Key Contribution**: Offline CoT evaluation/alignment with external structured feedback.\n- **Relevance**: Candidate offline evaluator for selecting robust trace regimes.\n\n### 10) Multi-Step Deductive Reasoning Over Natural Language (2022)\n- **Key Contribution**: Dedicated empirical OOD study for multi-step reasoning.\n- **Methodology**: IMA-GloVe-GA vs baselines on PARARULES/CONCEPTRULES; controlled OOD splits.\n- **Results**: Reported improvements over RNN baselines and stronger OOD behavior in deeper settings.\n- **Relevance**: Provides explicit OOD protocols transferable to LLM trace-length studies.\n\n### 11) Chain-of-Thought Reasoning is a Policy Improvement Operator (2023)\n- **Key Contribution**: Frames CoT as iterative policy improvement/self-learning.\n- **Relevance**: Theoretical rationale for adaptive iteration depth.\n\n### 12) Buffer of Thoughts (2024)\n- **Key Contribution**: Reusable thought templates for accuracy/efficiency/robustness.\n- **Relevance**: Structured trace compression and reuse; relevant to avoiding over-verbose traces.\n\n### 13) Is Chain-of-Thought Reasoning of LLMs a Mirage? A Data Distribution Lens (2025)\n- **Key Contribution**: Distribution-lens explanation of CoT success/failure.\n- **Methodology**: Controlled DataAlchemy setup with task/length/format shifts.\n- **Results**: Deep-read excerpts show strong in-distribution performance but severe degradation under composition, length, and format OOD; reports accuracy collapse under increased complexity.\n- **Relevance**: Strongest direct support for non-monotonic trace-length/robustness behavior.\n\n### 14) Slim-SC (2025)\n- **Key Contribution**: Thought pruning for efficient self-consistency.\n- **Relevance**: Explicit adaptive compute/length method to compare against fixed-k self-consistency.\n\n### 15) Sleep-time Compute (2025)\n- **Key Contribution**: Moves part of test-time reasoning compute offline.\n- **Relevance**: Alternative compute-allocation baseline when runtime trace expansion is expensive.\n\n### 16) Long CoT Survey (2025)\n- **Key Contribution**: Consolidates long-CoT methods, risks, and open problems.\n- **Relevance**: Context for trace-length scaling limits and safety/faithfulness issues.\n\n## Common Methodologies\n- Prompting-based trace elicitation: CoT few-shot/zero-shot and variants.\n- Sample-and-select: self-consistency, best-of-N reranking, verifier-guided selection.\n- Search-based inference: Tree-of-Thoughts/branching frameworks.\n- Process reward modeling: step-level supervision signals for filtering/reranking.\n- Controlled OOD probes: synthetic/compositional splits and cross-domain benchmarks.\n\n## Standard Baselines\n- Direct answer (no CoT)\n- Fixed CoT prompt with greedy decoding\n- Self-consistency with fixed sample count `k`\n- Majority voting over sampled traces\n- Outcome-supervised reward models (ORM)\n- Process-supervised reward models (PRM)\n\n## Evaluation Metrics\n- Primary: exact-match accuracy / problem solved rate\n- Robustness: in-distribution vs OOD delta, worst-group accuracy\n- Efficiency: tokens generated, latency, cost per correct answer\n- Selection quality: verifier agreement, pass@k / best-of-N curves\n\n## Datasets in the Literature\n- GSM8K, MATH/MATH-500, BBH, ARC-style QA\n- OOD-focused synthetic/compositional datasets (PARARULES, CONCEPTRULES, DataAlchemy-style controls)\n\n## Gaps and Opportunities\n- Limited direct measurement of **trace length as a continuous treatment variable** under fixed model weights.\n- Many works confound length with decoding strategy or model scale.\n- OOD robustness studies often focus on answer accuracy, not trace faithfulness/consistency jointly.\n- Adaptive stopping/pruning policies are promising but undercompared against strong fixed-length baselines across multiple task families.\n\n## Recommendations for Our Experiment\n- **Recommended datasets**: GSM8K, MATH-500, ARC-Challenge, BBH subset tasks, plus a controlled synthetic OOD generator.\n- **Recommended baselines**: direct answer, fixed CoT (short/medium/long), self-consistency (k={3,5,10,20}), ToT-style search, PRM/ORM reranking when available.\n- **Recommended metrics**: ID/OOD accuracy, robustness gap, token-cost efficiency, calibration/error-consistency under shift.\n- **Methodological considerations**:\n  - Sweep trace budgets at fixed model and prompt.\n  - Separate effects of verbosity from selection quality.\n  - Add uncertainty-triggered adaptive length control and compare to fixed policies at equal token budgets.\n'\"''')\n(root/'literature_review.md').write_text(lit)\n\n# resources.md\nres=textwrap.dedent('''\\\\\n# Resources Catalog\n\n## Summary\nThis document catalogs all resources gathered for the project on reasoning trace length and OOD robustness.\n\n### Search Strategy\n- Attempted \"'`paper-finder` diligent mode first; service timed out in this run.\n- Fallback: manual arXiv + Semantic Scholar API search with relevance filtering.\n- Downloaded foundational and recent papers covering CoT, process supervision, OOD analysis, and test-time compute.\n\n### Selection Criteria\n- Direct relevance to trace length, trace selection, or OOD robustness.\n- Inclusion of both foundational baselines and 2025 updates.\n- Preference for papers with available code/data or executable evaluation setup.\n\n## Papers\nTotal papers downloaded: 16\n\n| Title | Authors | Year | File | Key Info |\n|-------|---------|------|------|----------|\n| Chain-of-Thought Prompting Elicits Reasoning in LLMs | Wei et al. | 2022 | papers/2022_2201.11903v6_chain_of_thought_prompting_elicits_reasoning_in_la.pdf | Foundational CoT baseline |\n| Self-Consistency Improves CoT Reasoning | Wang et al. | 2022 | papers/2022_2203.11171v4_self_consistency_improves_chain_of_thought_reasoni.pdf | Multi-trace vote baseline |\n| Tree of Thoughts | Yao et al. | 2023 | papers/2023_2305.10601v2_tree_of_thoughts_deliberate_problem_solving_with_l.pdf | Search-based reasoning |\n| Let’s Verify Step by Step | Lightman et al. | 2023 | papers/2023_2305.20050v1_let_s_verify_step_by_step.pdf | PRM vs ORM; PRM800K |\n| Chain-of-Thought Hub | Fu et al. | 2023 | papers/2023_2305.17306v1_chain_of_thought_hub_a_continuous_effort_to_measur.pdf | Benchmark suite |\n| Math-Shepherd | Wang et al. | 2023 | papers/2023_2312.08935v3_math_shepherd_verify_and_reinforce_llms_step_by_st.pdf | Auto process reward |\n| Contrastive CoT Prompting | Chia et al. | 2023 | papers/2023_2311.09277v1_contrastive_chain_of_thought_prompting.pdf | Positive/negative traces |\n| GRACE | Khalifa et al. | 2023 | papers/2023_2305.14934v3_grace_discriminator_guided_chain_of_thought_reason.pdf | Discriminator-guided decoding |\n| OCEAN | Wu et al. | 2024 | papers/2024_2410.23703v1_ocean_offline_chain_of_thought_evaluation_and_alig.pdf | Offline CoT evaluator |\n| Multi-Step Deductive Reasoning OOD | Bao et al. | 2022 | papers/2022_2207.14000v4_multi_step_deductive_reasoning_over_natural_langua.pdf | Explicit OOD reasoning setup |\n| CoT as Policy Improvement | Zhang & Parkes | 2023 | papers/2023_2309.08589v2_chain_of_thought_reasoning_is_a_policy_improvement.pdf | Theoretical framing |\n| Buffer of Thoughts | Yang et al. | 2024 | papers/2024_2406.04271v2_buffer_of_thoughts_thought_augmented_reasoning_wit.pdf | Thought template memory |\n| Is CoT a Mirage? | Zhao et al. | 2025 | papers/2025_2508.01191v4_is_chain_of_thought_reasoning_of_llms_a_mirage_a_d.pdf | Distribution-lens failures |\n| Slim-SC | Hong et al. | 2025 | papers/2025_2509.13990v1_slim_sc_thought_pruning_for_efficient_scaling_with.pdf | Pruned self-consistency |\n| Sleep-time Compute | Lin et al. | 2025 | papers/2025_2504.13171v1_sleep_time_compute_beyond_inference_scaling_at_tes.pdf | Offline compute strategy |\n| Long CoT Survey | Chen et al. | 2025 | papers/2025_2503.09567v5_towards_reasoning_era_a_survey_of_long_chain_of_th.pdf | State-of-field survey |\n\nSee `papers/README.md` for detailed descriptions.\n\n## Datasets\nTotal datasets downloaded: 6\n\n| Name | Source | Size | Task | Location | Notes |\n|------|--------|------|------|----------|-------|\n| GSM8K | Hugging Face `gsm8k/main` | 7,473 train / 1,319 test | math reasoning | datasets/gsm8k_main/ | Baseline CoT benchmark |\n| MATH-500 | Hugging Face `HuggingFaceH4/MATH-500` | 500 test | hard math reasoning | datasets/math500/ | Hard-set robustness |\n| ARC-Challenge | Hugging Face `allenai/ai2_arc` | 1,119/299/1,172 | science QA reasoning | datasets/ai2_arc_challenge/ | Domain shift |\n| BBH: multistep_arithmetic_two | Hugging Face `lukaemon/bbh` | 250 test | symbolic/multi-step | datasets/bbh_multistep_arithmetic_two/ | OOD-style stress test |\n| BBH: logical_deduction_three_objects | Hugging Face `lukaemon/bbh` | 250 test | logical reasoning | datasets/bbh_logical_deduction_three_objects/ | Trace-quality sensitive |\n| BBH: date_understanding | Hugging Face `lukaemon/bbh` | 250 test | temporal reasoning | datasets/bbh_date_understanding/ | Diverse reasoning type |\n\nSee `datasets/README.md` for download/loading instructions.\n\n## Code Repositories\nTotal repositories cloned: 3\n\n| Name | URL | Purpose | Location | Notes |\n|------|-----|---------|----------|-------|\n| chain-of-thought-hub | https://github.com/FranxYao/chain-of-thought-hub | benchmark scripts/templates | code/chain-of-thought-hub/ | includes BBH, GSM8K, MMLU runners |\n| tree-of-thought-llm | https://github.com/princeton-nlp/tree-of-thought-llm | deliberate search inference | code/tree-of-thought-llm/ | ToT + BFS baseline |\n| prm800k | https://github.com/openai/prm800k | process supervision dataset + eval | code/prm800k/ | PRM/ORM evaluation utilities |\n\nSee `code/README.md` for details.\n\n## Resource Gathering Notes\n\n### Challenges Encountered\n- `paper-finder` service timed out, so manual API-based retrieval was used.\n- `uv add` failed because the workspace is not configured as an installable package; fallback to `uv pip install` succeeded.\n- `hendrycks/competition_math` dataset identifier was unavailable on HF; replaced with `MATH-500` plus additional BBH tasks.\n\n### Gaps and Workarounds\n- No single canonical OOD dataset for trace-length studies; combined math + science + BBH tasks and recommend adding a synthetic controlled OOD generator for final experiments.\n\n## Recommendations for Experiment Design\n\n1. **Primary datasets**: GSM8K + MATH-500 for core reasoning; BBH+ARC for distribution shift.\n2. **Baseline methods**: direct answer, fixed-length CoT, self-consistency, ToT, verifier/reranker methods.\n3. **Evaluation metrics**: ID/OOD accuracy, robustness gap, token cost, calibration/error-consistency.\n4. **Code to adapt**: use `chain-of-thought-hub` for benchmark plumbing, `tree-of-thought-llm` for adaptive search, and `prm800k` for process-supervision/verifier pipelines.\n'\"''')\n(root/'resources.md').write_text(res)\n\nprint('Wrote documentation files.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"source .venv/bin/activate && python - << 'PY'\nimport json, os, datetime, pathlib, textwrap\nroot=pathlib.Path('.')\nmeta=json.load(open('artifacts/selected_papers_metadata.json'))\nds_summary=json.load(open('artifacts/dataset_summary.json'))\n\nrelevance={\n'Chain-of-Thought Prompting Elicits Reasoning in Large Language Models':'Foundational CoT prompting baseline and emergence behavior.',\n'Self-Consistency Improves Chain of Thought Reasoning in Language Models':'Canonical test-time compute baseline (sample multiple traces + vote).',\n'Tree of Thoughts: Deliberate Problem Solving with Large Language Models':'Structured search over reasoning traces; useful for adaptive trace budgeting.',\n\\\"Let's Verify Step by Step\\\":'Key process-supervision paper; directly links step-level supervision to robustness and OOD.',\n\\\"Chain-of-Thought Hub: A Continuous Effort to Measure Large Language Models' Reasoning Performance\\\":'Benchmark suite spanning GSM8K/MATH/BBH/MMLU for reasoning evaluation.',\n'Math-Shepherd: Verify and Reinforce LLMs Step-by-step without Human Annotations':'Automatic process reward construction; practical alternative to expensive human labels.',\n'Contrastive Chain-of-Thought Prompting':'Demonstrates learning from incorrect reasoning contrastively.',\n'GRACE: Discriminator-Guided Chain-of-Thought Reasoning':'Step-level discriminator guidance; helps reduce wrong reasoning branches.',\n'OCEAN: Offline Chain-of-thought Evaluation and Alignment in Large Language Models':'Offline CoT evaluator/alignment paradigm; relevant for verifier-based selection.',\n'Multi-Step Deductive Reasoning Over Natural Language: An Empirical Study on Out-of-Distribution Generalisation':'Direct OOD generalization study in multi-step reasoning.',\n'Chain-of-Thought Reasoning is a Policy Improvement Operator':'Theoretical/algorithmic framing of CoT as iterative policy improvement.',\n'Buffer of Thoughts: Thought-Augmented Reasoning with Large Language Models':'Template-buffer approach trading off quality and efficiency.',\n'Is Chain-of-Thought Reasoning of LLMs a Mirage? A Data Distribution Lens':'Strong evidence for distribution-dependent/non-monotonic CoT behavior.',\n'Slim-SC: Thought Pruning for Efficient Scaling with Self-Consistency':'Adaptive pruning for self-consistency, central to length/compute control.',\n'Sleep-time Compute: Beyond Inference Scaling at Test-time':'Alternative compute allocation (offline precomputation) for reasoning tasks.',\n'Towards Reasoning Era: A Survey of Long Chain-of-Thought for Reasoning Large Language Models':'Survey of long-CoT methods, risks, and open problems.',\n}\n\n# papers README\nlines=['# Downloaded Papers','']\nfor i,p in enumerate(meta,1):\n    fn=os.path.basename(p['file'])\n    arxiv=(p.get('id') or '').replace('v','') if p.get('id') else 'N/A'\n    lines.append(f\\\"{i}. [{p['title']}]({fn})\\\")\n    lines.append(f\\\"   - Authors: {', '.join(p.get('authors',[])[:8])}{' et al.' if len(p.get('authors',[]))>8 else ''}\\\")\n    lines.append(f\\\"   - Year: {p.get('year')}\\\")\n    lines.append(f\\\"   - arXiv: {p.get('url')}\\\")\n    lines.append(f\\\"   - Why relevant: {relevance.get(p['title'],'Relevant to reasoning trace control and robustness.')}\\\")\n    lines.append('')\n(root/'papers'/'README.md').write_text('\\\\n'.join(lines))\n\n# datasets .gitignore\n(root/'datasets'/'.gitignore').write_text(textwrap.dedent('''\\\\\n# Exclude all data files (can be large)\n*\n\n# But include documentation and small samples\n\"'!.gitignore\n!README.md\n!**/README.md\n!**/samples/\n!**/samples/**\n!**/download.sh\n!**/download_instructions.txt\n'\"'''))\n\n# datasets README\nds_readme=textwrap.dedent('''\\\\\n# Downloaded Datasets\n\nThis directory contains datasets for the research project. Large data files are not intended for git commits; keep them local and rely on the instructions below for reproducibility.\n\n## Dataset 1: GSM8K\n\n### Overview\n- **Source**: \"'`gsm8k` (`main` config) on Hugging Face\n- **Size**: train 7,473; test 1,319\n- **Format**: HuggingFace DatasetDict\n- **Task**: Math word-problem reasoning\n- **Splits**: train/test\n- **License**: Check dataset card on Hugging Face\n\n### Download Instructions\n\n**Using HuggingFace (recommended):**\n```python\nfrom datasets import load_dataset\ndataset = load_dataset(\"gsm8k\", \"main\")\ndataset.save_to_disk(\"datasets/gsm8k_main\")\n```\n\n### Loading the Dataset\n```python\nfrom datasets import load_from_disk\ndataset = load_from_disk(\"datasets/gsm8k_main\")\n```\n\n### Sample Data\nStored at `datasets/gsm8k_main/samples/samples.json`.\n\n### Notes\n- Strong base benchmark for chain-of-thought length and self-consistency studies.\n\n## Dataset 2: MATH-500\n\n### Overview\n- **Source**: `HuggingFaceH4/MATH-500`\n- **Size**: test 500\n- **Format**: HuggingFace DatasetDict\n- **Task**: Competition-level mathematical reasoning\n- **Splits**: test\n- **License**: Check dataset card on Hugging Face\n\n### Download Instructions\n\n**Using HuggingFace (recommended):**\n```python\nfrom datasets import load_dataset\ndataset = load_dataset(\"HuggingFaceH4/MATH-500\")\ndataset.save_to_disk(\"datasets/math500\")\n```\n\n### Loading the Dataset\n```python\nfrom datasets import load_from_disk\ndataset = load_from_disk(\"datasets/math500\")\n```\n\n### Sample Data\nStored at `datasets/math500/samples/samples.json`.\n\n### Notes\n- Useful hard evaluation set for testing whether optimal trace length shifts with problem difficulty.\n\n## Dataset 3: ARC-Challenge\n\n### Overview\n- **Source**: `allenai/ai2_arc` (`ARC-Challenge` config)\n- **Size**: train 1,119; validation 299; test 1,172\n- **Format**: HuggingFace DatasetDict\n- **Task**: Science QA reasoning / transfer-style robustness check\n- **Splits**: train/validation/test\n- **License**: Check dataset card on Hugging Face\n\n### Download Instructions\n\n**Using HuggingFace (recommended):**\n```python\nfrom datasets import load_dataset\ndataset = load_dataset(\"allenai/ai2_arc\", \"ARC-Challenge\")\ndataset.save_to_disk(\"datasets/ai2_arc_challenge\")\n```\n\n### Loading the Dataset\n```python\nfrom datasets import load_from_disk\ndataset = load_from_disk(\"datasets/ai2_arc_challenge\")\n```\n\n### Sample Data\nStored at `datasets/ai2_arc_challenge/samples/samples.json`.\n\n### Notes\n- Adds non-math domain shift, useful for OOD robustness tests.\n\n## Dataset 4-6: BBH Subset Tasks\n\n### Overview\n- **Source**: `lukaemon/bbh`\n- **Configs downloaded**: `multistep_arithmetic_two`, `logical_deduction_three_objects`, `date_understanding`\n- **Size**: each test split has 250 examples\n- **Format**: HuggingFace DatasetDict\n- **Task**: Diverse compositional reasoning stress tests\n\n### Download Instructions\n\n**Using HuggingFace (recommended):**\n```python\nfrom datasets import load_dataset\nfor cfg in [\n    \"multistep_arithmetic_two\",\n    \"logical_deduction_three_objects\",\n    \"date_understanding\",\n]:\n    ds = load_dataset(\"lukaemon/bbh\", cfg)\n    ds.save_to_disk(f\"datasets/bbh_{cfg}\")\n```\n\n### Loading the Dataset\n```python\nfrom datasets import load_from_disk\ndataset = load_from_disk(\"datasets/bbh_multistep_arithmetic_two\")\n```\n\n### Sample Data\nStored in each dataset folder under `samples/samples.json`.\n\n### Notes\n- BBH provides task diversity to test whether trace-length optima are task-dependent.\n'\"''')\n(root/'datasets'/'README.md').write_text(ds_readme)\n\n# code README\ncode_readme=textwrap.dedent('''\\\\\n# Cloned Repositories\n\n## Repo 1: chain-of-thought-hub\n- URL: https://github.com/FranxYao/chain-of-thought-hub\n- Purpose: Multi-benchmark CoT evaluation suite (GSM8K, MATH, BBH, MMLU).\n- Location: \"'`code/chain-of-thought-hub/`\n- Key files:\n  - `readme.md`\n  - `BBH/run_bbh.py`\n  - `MMLU/run_mmlu_open_source.py`\n- Notes: Provides prompt templates and benchmark runners useful for fixed-length and sampled-CoT baselines.\n\n## Repo 2: tree-of-thought-llm\n- URL: https://github.com/princeton-nlp/tree-of-thought-llm\n- Purpose: Official Tree-of-Thoughts implementation for deliberate inference-time search.\n- Location: `code/tree-of-thought-llm/`\n- Key files:\n  - `run.py`\n  - `scripts/game24/*.sh`\n  - `src/tot/`\n- Notes: Useful for adaptive reasoning budget baselines (branching/search depth controls).\n\n## Repo 3: prm800k\n- URL: https://github.com/openai/prm800k\n- Purpose: PRM800K process-supervision labels and evaluation logic from “Let’s Verify Step by Step”.\n- Location: `code/prm800k/`\n- Key files:\n  - `README.md`\n  - `prm800k/data/`\n  - `prm800k/eval/eval.py`\n- Notes: Includes step-level supervision data format, grading scripts, and PRM-vs-ORM evaluation setup.\n'\"''')\n(root/'code'/'README.md').write_text(code_readme)\n\n# literature_review.md\nlit=textwrap.dedent('''\\\\\n# Literature Review: Reasoning Trace Length as a Proxy for Robustness\n\n## Review Scope\n\n### Research Question\nHow does reasoning trace length affect OOD robustness in LLM reasoning, and can adaptive trace-length control outperform fixed-length strategies?\n\n### Inclusion Criteria\n- Studies on chain-of-thought, trace control, process supervision, verifier-guided reasoning, or test-time reasoning compute.\n- Studies reporting reasoning benchmark results (GSM8K, MATH, BBH, ARC-like transfers).\n- OOD/distribution-shift analyses or efficiency-accuracy tradeoff analyses.\n\n### Exclusion Criteria\n- Purely non-LLM symbolic systems without relevance to modern LLM trace control.\n- Papers lacking empirical evidence or clear methodological detail.\n\n### Time Frame\n2022-2025 (plus foundational context where required).\n\n### Sources\n- arXiv API (primary)\n- Semantic Scholar API (supplementary)\n- Paper-finder script attempted but service timed out in this run\n\n## Search Log\n\n| Date | Query | Source | Results | Notes |\n|------|-------|--------|---------|-------|\n| 2026-04-06 | \\\"Reasoning Trace Length as a Proxy for Robustness ...\\\" | paper-finder script | timeout | Fallback to manual APIs |\n| 2026-04-06 | chain of thought length / OOD reasoning / test-time compute | arXiv API | 100+ candidates | deduplicated and ranked |\n| 2026-04-06 | CoT robustness / OOD generalization | Semantic Scholar API | merged into candidate pool | used for citation/context |\n\n## Screening Results\n\n- Title/abstract screened: 101\n- Full PDFs downloaded: 16\n- Deep-read (all chunk PDFs):\n  - \"'`Let’s Verify Step by Step` (10 chunks)\n  - `Multi-Step Deductive Reasoning... OOD Generalisation` (6 chunks)\n  - `Is CoT a Mirage?` (13 chunks)\n\n## Key Papers\n\n### 1) Chain-of-Thought Prompting Elicits Reasoning in Large Language Models (2022)\n- **Key Contribution**: Establishes CoT prompting as a major reasoning boost.\n- **Methodology**: Few-shot CoT exemplars.\n- **Datasets**: Standard reasoning benchmarks (math/commonsense).\n- **Results**: Large gains vs direct answer prompting.\n- **Relevance**: Defines the baseline trace-length intervention.\n\n### 2) Self-Consistency Improves Chain of Thought Reasoning in Language Models (2022)\n- **Key Contribution**: Replaces greedy single-trace decoding with multi-trace sampling + voting.\n- **Methodology**: Sample diverse traces; marginalize answers.\n- **Datasets**: GSM8K, SVAMP, AQuA, StrategyQA, ARC-style sets (per paper).\n- **Results**: Stronger reasoning accuracy with added test-time compute.\n- **Relevance**: Central fixed-compute/variable-trace baseline for this project.\n\n### 3) Tree of Thoughts (2023)\n- **Key Contribution**: Search over thought states instead of pure left-to-right generation.\n- **Methodology**: Deliberate branching/evaluation/selection.\n- **Results**: Improved outcomes on planning/search-heavy tasks.\n- **Relevance**: Natural adaptive-length/control baseline.\n\n### 4) Let’s Verify Step by Step (2023)\n- **Key Contribution**: Process supervision outperforms outcome supervision.\n- **Methodology**: PRM vs ORM; step-level human labels (PRM800K), best-of-N search evaluation.\n- **Datasets Used**: MATH + held-out STEM OOD tests (AP Physics/Calculus/Chemistry, AMC10/12).\n- **Results**: Deep-read excerpts indicate PRM reaches ~78% solved on representative MATH subset and consistently beats ORM/majority-vote baselines; better OOD behavior than ORM.\n- **Relevance**: Direct evidence that *quality and selection* of traces matters more than raw verbosity.\n\n### 5) Chain-of-Thought Hub (2023)\n- **Key Contribution**: Open benchmark stack for reasoning models and prompts.\n- **Methodology**: Unified evaluation across GSM8K/MATH/BBH/MMLU etc.\n- **Relevance**: Practical infrastructure for controlled trace-length experiments.\n\n### 6) Math-Shepherd (2023)\n- **Key Contribution**: Automatic process reward model training without expensive human labeling.\n- **Relevance**: Scalable process-verifier signal for adaptive trace filtering.\n\n### 7) Contrastive Chain-of-Thought Prompting (2023)\n- **Key Contribution**: Uses negative reasoning examples to reduce typical CoT mistakes.\n- **Relevance**: Supports the view that trace content quality, not just length, drives robustness.\n\n### 8) GRACE (2023)\n- **Key Contribution**: Step-level correctness discriminator guides decoding.\n- **Relevance**: Verifier-guided adaptive pruning strategy.\n\n### 9) OCEAN (2024)\n- **Key Contribution**: Offline CoT evaluation/alignment with external structured feedback.\n- **Relevance**: Candidate offline evaluator for selecting robust trace regimes.\n\n### 10) Multi-Step Deductive Reasoning Over Natural Language (2022)\n- **Key Contribution**: Dedicated empirical OOD study for multi-step reasoning.\n- **Methodology**: IMA-GloVe-GA vs baselines on PARARULES/CONCEPTRULES; controlled OOD splits.\n- **Results**: Reported improvements over RNN baselines and stronger OOD behavior in deeper settings.\n- **Relevance**: Provides explicit OOD protocols transferable to LLM trace-length studies.\n\n### 11) Chain-of-Thought Reasoning is a Policy Improvement Operator (2023)\n- **Key Contribution**: Frames CoT as iterative policy improvement/self-learning.\n- **Relevance**: Theoretical rationale for adaptive iteration depth.\n\n### 12) Buffer of Thoughts (2024)\n- **Key Contribution**: Reusable thought templates for accuracy/efficiency/robustness.\n- **Relevance**: Structured trace compression and reuse; relevant to avoiding over-verbose traces.\n\n### 13) Is Chain-of-Thought Reasoning of LLMs a Mirage? A Data Distribution Lens (2025)\n- **Key Contribution**: Distribution-lens explanation of CoT success/failure.\n- **Methodology**: Controlled DataAlchemy setup with task/length/format shifts.\n- **Results**: Deep-read excerpts show strong in-distribution performance but severe degradation under composition, length, and format OOD; reports accuracy collapse under increased complexity.\n- **Relevance**: Strongest direct support for non-monotonic trace-length/robustness behavior.\n\n### 14) Slim-SC (2025)\n- **Key Contribution**: Thought pruning for efficient self-consistency.\n- **Relevance**: Explicit adaptive compute/length method to compare against fixed-k self-consistency.\n\n### 15) Sleep-time Compute (2025)\n- **Key Contribution**: Moves part of test-time reasoning compute offline.\n- **Relevance**: Alternative compute-allocation baseline when runtime trace expansion is expensive.\n\n### 16) Long CoT Survey (2025)\n- **Key Contribution**: Consolidates long-CoT methods, risks, and open problems.\n- **Relevance**: Context for trace-length scaling limits and safety/faithfulness issues.\n\n## Common Methodologies\n- Prompting-based trace elicitation: CoT few-shot/zero-shot and variants.\n- Sample-and-select: self-consistency, best-of-N reranking, verifier-guided selection.\n- Search-based inference: Tree-of-Thoughts/branching frameworks.\n- Process reward modeling: step-level supervision signals for filtering/reranking.\n- Controlled OOD probes: synthetic/compositional splits and cross-domain benchmarks.\n\n## Standard Baselines\n- Direct answer (no CoT)\n- Fixed CoT prompt with greedy decoding\n- Self-consistency with fixed sample count `k`\n- Majority voting over sampled traces\n- Outcome-supervised reward models (ORM)\n- Process-supervised reward models (PRM)\n\n## Evaluation Metrics\n- Primary: exact-match accuracy / problem solved rate\n- Robustness: in-distribution vs OOD delta, worst-group accuracy\n- Efficiency: tokens generated, latency, cost per correct answer\n- Selection quality: verifier agreement, pass@k / best-of-N curves\n\n## Datasets in the Literature\n- GSM8K, MATH/MATH-500, BBH, ARC-style QA\n- OOD-focused synthetic/compositional datasets (PARARULES, CONCEPTRULES, DataAlchemy-style controls)\n\n## Gaps and Opportunities\n- Limited direct measurement of **trace length as a continuous treatment variable** under fixed model weights.\n- Many works confound length with decoding strategy or model scale.\n- OOD robustness studies often focus on answer accuracy, not trace faithfulness/consistency jointly.\n- Adaptive stopping/pruning policies are promising but undercompared against strong fixed-length baselines across multiple task families.\n\n## Recommendations for Our Experiment\n- **Recommended datasets**: GSM8K, MATH-500, ARC-Challenge, BBH subset tasks, plus a controlled synthetic OOD generator.\n- **Recommended baselines**: direct answer, fixed CoT (short/medium/long), self-consistency (k={3,5,10,20}), ToT-style search, PRM/ORM reranking when available.\n- **Recommended metrics**: ID/OOD accuracy, robustness gap, token-cost efficiency, calibration/error-consistency under shift.\n- **Methodological considerations**:\n  - Sweep trace budgets at fixed model and prompt.\n  - Separate effects of verbosity from selection quality.\n  - Add uncertainty-triggered adaptive length control and compare to fixed policies at equal token budgets.\n'\"''')\n(root/'literature_review.md').write_text(lit)\n\n# resources.md\nres=textwrap.dedent('''\\\\\n# Resources Catalog\n\n## Summary\nThis document catalogs all resources gathered for the project on reasoning trace length and OOD robustness.\n\n### Search Strategy\n- Attempted \"'`paper-finder` diligent mode first; service timed out in this run.\n- Fallback: manual arXiv + Semantic Scholar API search with relevance filtering.\n- Downloaded foundational and recent papers covering CoT, process supervision, OOD analysis, and test-time compute.\n\n### Selection Criteria\n- Direct relevance to trace length, trace selection, or OOD robustness.\n- Inclusion of both foundational baselines and 2025 updates.\n- Preference for papers with available code/data or executable evaluation setup.\n\n## Papers\nTotal papers downloaded: 16\n\n| Title | Authors | Year | File | Key Info |\n|-------|---------|------|------|----------|\n| Chain-of-Thought Prompting Elicits Reasoning in LLMs | Wei et al. | 2022 | papers/2022_2201.11903v6_chain_of_thought_prompting_elicits_reasoning_in_la.pdf | Foundational CoT baseline |\n| Self-Consistency Improves CoT Reasoning | Wang et al. | 2022 | papers/2022_2203.11171v4_self_consistency_improves_chain_of_thought_reasoni.pdf | Multi-trace vote baseline |\n| Tree of Thoughts | Yao et al. | 2023 | papers/2023_2305.10601v2_tree_of_thoughts_deliberate_problem_solving_with_l.pdf | Search-based reasoning |\n| Let’s Verify Step by Step | Lightman et al. | 2023 | papers/2023_2305.20050v1_let_s_verify_step_by_step.pdf | PRM vs ORM; PRM800K |\n| Chain-of-Thought Hub | Fu et al. | 2023 | papers/2023_2305.17306v1_chain_of_thought_hub_a_continuous_effort_to_measur.pdf | Benchmark suite |\n| Math-Shepherd | Wang et al. | 2023 | papers/2023_2312.08935v3_math_shepherd_verify_and_reinforce_llms_step_by_st.pdf | Auto process reward |\n| Contrastive CoT Prompting | Chia et al. | 2023 | papers/2023_2311.09277v1_contrastive_chain_of_thought_prompting.pdf | Positive/negative traces |\n| GRACE | Khalifa et al. | 2023 | papers/2023_2305.14934v3_grace_discriminator_guided_chain_of_thought_reason.pdf | Discriminator-guided decoding |\n| OCEAN | Wu et al. | 2024 | papers/2024_2410.23703v1_ocean_offline_chain_of_thought_evaluation_and_alig.pdf | Offline CoT evaluator |\n| Multi-Step Deductive Reasoning OOD | Bao et al. | 2022 | papers/2022_2207.14000v4_multi_step_deductive_reasoning_over_natural_langua.pdf | Explicit OOD reasoning setup |\n| CoT as Policy Improvement | Zhang & Parkes | 2023 | papers/2023_2309.08589v2_chain_of_thought_reasoning_is_a_policy_improvement.pdf | Theoretical framing |\n| Buffer of Thoughts | Yang et al. | 2024 | papers/2024_2406.04271v2_buffer_of_thoughts_thought_augmented_reasoning_wit.pdf | Thought template memory |\n| Is CoT a Mirage? | Zhao et al. | 2025 | papers/2025_2508.01191v4_is_chain_of_thought_reasoning_of_llms_a_mirage_a_d.pdf | Distribution-lens failures |\n| Slim-SC | Hong et al. | 2025 | papers/2025_2509.13990v1_slim_sc_thought_pruning_for_efficient_scaling_with.pdf | Pruned self-consistency |\n| Sleep-time Compute | Lin et al. | 2025 | papers/2025_2504.13171v1_sleep_time_compute_beyond_inference_scaling_at_tes.pdf | Offline compute strategy |\n| Long CoT Survey | Chen et al. | 2025 | papers/2025_2503.09567v5_towards_reasoning_era_a_survey_of_long_chain_of_th.pdf | State-of-field survey |\n\nSee `papers/README.md` for detailed descriptions.\n\n## Datasets\nTotal datasets downloaded: 6\n\n| Name | Source | Size | Task | Location | Notes |\n|------|--------|------|------|----------|-------|\n| GSM8K | Hugging Face `gsm8k/main` | 7,473 train / 1,319 test | math reasoning | datasets/gsm8k_main/ | Baseline CoT benchmark |\n| MATH-500 | Hugging Face `HuggingFaceH4/MATH-500` | 500 test | hard math reasoning | datasets/math500/ | Hard-set robustness |\n| ARC-Challenge | Hugging Face `allenai/ai2_arc` | 1,119/299/1,172 | science QA reasoning | datasets/ai2_arc_challenge/ | Domain shift |\n| BBH: multistep_arithmetic_two | Hugging Face `lukaemon/bbh` | 250 test | symbolic/multi-step | datasets/bbh_multistep_arithmetic_two/ | OOD-style stress test |\n| BBH: logical_deduction_three_objects | Hugging Face `lukaemon/bbh` | 250 test | logical reasoning | datasets/bbh_logical_deduction_three_objects/ | Trace-quality sensitive |\n| BBH: date_understanding | Hugging Face `lukaemon/bbh` | 250 test | temporal reasoning | datasets/bbh_date_understanding/ | Diverse reasoning type |\n\nSee `datasets/README.md` for download/loading instructions.\n\n## Code Repositories\nTotal repositories cloned: 3\n\n| Name | URL | Purpose | Location | Notes |\n|------|-----|---------|----------|-------|\n| chain-of-thought-hub | https://github.com/FranxYao/chain-of-thought-hub | benchmark scripts/templates | code/chain-of-thought-hub/ | includes BBH, GSM8K, MMLU runners |\n| tree-of-thought-llm | https://github.com/princeton-nlp/tree-of-thought-llm | deliberate search inference | code/tree-of-thought-llm/ | ToT + BFS baseline |\n| prm800k | https://github.com/openai/prm800k | process supervision dataset + eval | code/prm800k/ | PRM/ORM evaluation utilities |\n\nSee `code/README.md` for details.\n\n## Resource Gathering Notes\n\n### Challenges Encountered\n- `paper-finder` service timed out, so manual API-based retrieval was used.\n- `uv add` failed because the workspace is not configured as an installable package; fallback to `uv pip install` succeeded.\n- `hendrycks/competition_math` dataset identifier was unavailable on HF; replaced with `MATH-500` plus additional BBH tasks.\n\n### Gaps and Workarounds\n- No single canonical OOD dataset for trace-length studies; combined math + science + BBH tasks and recommend adding a synthetic controlled OOD generator for final experiments.\n\n## Recommendations for Experiment Design\n\n1. **Primary datasets**: GSM8K + MATH-500 for core reasoning; BBH+ARC for distribution shift.\n2. **Baseline methods**: direct answer, fixed-length CoT, self-consistency, ToT, verifier/reranker methods.\n3. **Evaluation metrics**: ID/OOD accuracy, robustness gap, token cost, calibration/error-consistency.\n4. **Code to adapt**: use `chain-of-thought-hub` for benchmark plumbing, `tree-of-thought-llm` for adaptive search, and `prm800k` for process-supervision/verifier pipelines.\n'\"''')\n(root/'resources.md').write_text(res)\n\nprint('Wrote documentation files.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"Wrote documentation files.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
