{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' papers/README.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Downloaded Papers\n\n1. [Chain-of-Thought Prompting Elicits Reasoning in Large Language Models](2022_2201.11903v6_chain_of_thought_prompting_elicits_reasoning_in_la.pdf)\n   - Authors: Jason Wei, Xuezhi Wang, Dale Schuurmans, Maarten Bosma, Brian Ichter, Fei Xia, Ed Chi, Quoc Le et al.\n   - Year: 2022\n   - arXiv: http://arxiv.org/abs/2201.11903v6\n   - Why relevant: Foundational CoT prompting baseline and emergence behavior.\n\n2. [Self-Consistency Improves Chain of Thought Reasoning in Language Models](2022_2203.11171v4_self_consistency_improves_chain_of_thought_reasoni.pdf)\n   - Authors: Xuezhi Wang, Jason Wei, Dale Schuurmans, Quoc Le, Ed Chi, Sharan Narang, Aakanksha Chowdhery, Denny Zhou\n   - Year: 2022\n   - arXiv: http://arxiv.org/abs/2203.11171v4\n   - Why relevant: Canonical test-time compute baseline (sample multiple traces + vote).\n\n3. [Tree of Thoughts: Deliberate Problem Solving with Large Language Models](2023_2305.10601v2_tree_of_thoughts_deliberate_problem_solving_with_l.pdf)\n   - Authors: Shunyu Yao, Dian Yu, Jeffrey Zhao, Izhak Shafran, Thomas L. Griffiths, Yuan Cao, Karthik Narasimhan\n   - Year: 2023\n   - arXiv: http://arxiv.org/abs/2305.10601v2\n   - Why relevant: Structured search over reasoning traces; useful for adaptive trace budgeting.\n\n4. [Let's Verify Step by Step](2023_2305.20050v1_let_s_verify_step_by_step.pdf)\n   - Authors: Hunter Lightman, Vineet Kosaraju, Yura Burda, Harri Edwards, Bowen Baker, Teddy Lee, Jan Leike, John Schulman et al.\n   - Year: 2023\n   - arXiv: http://arxiv.org/abs/2305.20050v1\n   - Why relevant: Key process-supervision paper; directly links step-level supervision to robustness and OOD.\n\n5. [Chain-of-Thought Hub: A Continuous Effort to Measure Large Language Models' Reasoning Performance](2023_2305.17306v1_chain_of_thought_hub_a_continuous_effort_to_measur.pdf)\n   - Authors: Yao Fu, Litu Ou, Mingyu Chen, Yuhao Wan, Hao Peng, Tushar Khot\n   - Year: 2023\n   - arXiv: http://arxiv.org/abs/2305.17306v1\n   - Why relevant: Benchmark suite spanning GSM8K/MATH/BBH/MMLU for reasoning evaluation.\n\n6. [Math-Shepherd: Verify and Reinforce LLMs Step-by-step without Human Annotations](2023_2312.08935v3_math_shepherd_verify_and_reinforce_llms_step_by_st.pdf)\n   - Authors: Peiyi Wang, Lei Li, Zhihong Shao, R. X. Xu, Damai Dai, Yifei Li, Deli Chen, Y. Wu et al.\n   - Year: 2023\n   - arXiv: http://arxiv.org/abs/2312.08935v3\n   - Why relevant: Automatic process reward construction; practical alternative to expensive human labels.\n\n7. [Contrastive Chain-of-Thought Prompting](2023_2311.09277v1_contrastive_chain_of_thought_prompting.pdf)\n   - Authors: Yew Ken Chia, Guizhen Chen, Luu Anh Tuan, Soujanya Poria, Lidong Bing\n   - Year: 2023\n   - arXiv: http://arxiv.org/abs/2311.09277v1\n   - Why relevant: Demonstrates learning from incorrect reasoning contrastively.\n\n8. [GRACE: Discriminator-Guided Chain-of-Thought Reasoning](2023_2305.14934v3_grace_discriminator_guided_chain_of_thought_reason.pdf)\n   - Authors: Muhammad Khalifa, Lajanugen Logeswaran, Moontae Lee, Honglak Lee, Lu Wang\n   - Year: 2023\n   - arXiv: http://arxiv.org/abs/2305.14934v3\n   - Why relevant: Step-level discriminator guidance; helps reduce wrong reasoning branches.\n\n9. [OCEAN: Offline Chain-of-thought Evaluation and Alignment in Large Language Models](2024_2410.23703v1_ocean_offline_chain_of_thought_evaluation_and_alig.pdf)\n   - Authors: Junda Wu, Xintong Li, Ruoyu Wang, Yu Xia, Yuxin Xiong, Jianing Wang, Tong Yu, Xiang Chen et al.\n   - Year: 2024\n   - arXiv: http://arxiv.org/abs/2410.23703v1\n   - Why relevant: Offline CoT evaluator/alignment paradigm; relevant for verifier-based selection.\n\n10. [Multi-Step Deductive Reasoning Over Natural Language: An Empirical Study on Out-of-Distribution Generalisation](2022_2207.14000v4_multi_step_deductive_reasoning_over_natural_langua.pdf)\n   - Authors: Qiming Bao, Alex Yuxuan Peng, Tim Hartill, Neset Tan, Zhenyun Deng, Michael Witbrock, Jiamou Liu\n   - Year: 2022\n   - arXiv: http://arxiv.org/abs/2207.14000v4\n   - Why relevant: Direct OOD generalization study in multi-step reasoning.\n\n11. [Chain-of-Thought Reasoning is a Policy Improvement Operator](2023_2309.08589v2_chain_of_thought_reasoning_is_a_policy_improvement.pdf)\n   - Authors: Hugh Zhang, David C. Parkes\n   - Year: 2023\n   - arXiv: http://arxiv.org/abs/2309.08589v2\n   - Why relevant: Theoretical/algorithmic framing of CoT as iterative policy improvement.\n\n12. [Buffer of Thoughts: Thought-Augmented Reasoning with Large Language Models](2024_2406.04271v2_buffer_of_thoughts_thought_augmented_reasoning_wit.pdf)\n   - Authors: Ling Yang, Zhaochen Yu, Tianjun Zhang, Shiyi Cao, Minkai Xu, Wentao Zhang, Joseph E. Gonzalez, Bin Cui\n   - Year: 2024\n   - arXiv: http://arxiv.org/abs/2406.04271v2\n   - Why relevant: Template-buffer approach trading off quality and efficiency.\n\n13. [Is Chain-of-Thought Reasoning of LLMs a Mirage? A Data Distribution Lens](2025_2508.01191v4_is_chain_of_thought_reasoning_of_llms_a_mirage_a_d.pdf)\n   - Authors: Chengshuai Zhao, Zhen Tan, Pingchuan Ma, Dawei Li, Bohan Jiang, Yancheng Wang, Yingzhen Yang, Huan Liu\n   - Year: 2025\n   - arXiv: http://arxiv.org/abs/2508.01191v4\n   - Why relevant: Strong evidence for distribution-dependent/non-monotonic CoT behavior.\n\n14. [Slim-SC: Thought Pruning for Efficient Scaling with Self-Consistency](2025_2509.13990v1_slim_sc_thought_pruning_for_efficient_scaling_with.pdf)\n   - Authors: Colin Hong, Xu Guo, Anand Chaanan Singh, Esha Choukse, Dmitrii Ustiugov\n   - Year: 2025\n   - arXiv: http://arxiv.org/abs/2509.13990v1\n   - Why relevant: Adaptive pruning for self-consistency, central to length/compute control.\n\n15. [Sleep-time Compute: Beyond Inference Scaling at Test-time](2025_2504.13171v1_sleep_time_compute_beyond_inference_scaling_at_tes.pdf)\n   - Authors: Kevin Lin, Charlie Snell, Yu Wang, Charles Packer, Sarah Wooders, Ion Stoica, Joseph E. Gonzalez\n   - Year: 2025\n   - arXiv: http://arxiv.org/abs/2504.13171v1\n   - Why relevant: Alternative compute allocation (offline precomputation) for reasoning tasks.\n\n16. [Towards Reasoning Era: A Survey of Long Chain-of-Thought for Reasoning Large Language Models](2025_2503.09567v5_towards_reasoning_era_a_survey_of_long_chain_of_th.pdf)\n   - Authors: Qiguang Chen, Libo Qin, Jinhao Liu, Dengyun Peng, Jiannan Guan, Peng Wang, Mengkang Hu, Yuhang Zhou et al.\n   - Year: 2025\n   - arXiv: http://arxiv.org/abs/2503.09567v5\n   - Why relevant: Survey of long-CoT methods, risks, and open problems.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
